msgstr "启用原本由 `PYTEST_IGNORED_TESTS` 和 `PYTEST_BROKEN_TESTS` 忽略的测试。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2352
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`python`"
msgstr "`python`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2355
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Possible arguments: (none), `_X.Y_`, `_X.Y+_`, `_-X.Y_`, `_X.Y-Z.A_`, "
"`patch`, `build`, `run`, `test`"
msgstr "可能的参数：（无）、`_X.Y_`、`_X.Y+_`、`_-X.Y_`、`_X.Y-Z.A_`、`patch`、`build`、`run`、`test`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2360
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Uses Python. A supported version or version range can be specified.  If "
"Python is only needed at build time, run time or for the tests, it can be "
"set as a build, run or test dependency with `build`, `run`, or `test`.  If "
"Python is also needed during the patch phase, use `patch`.  See crossref:"
"special[using-python, Using Python] for more information."
msgstr "使用 Python。可以指定受支持的版本或版本范围。如果仅在构建时、运行时或测试时需要 Python，可以通过 `build`、`run` 或 `test` 将其设为相应的依赖。如果在打补丁阶段也需要 Python，请使用 `patch`。更多信息请参见 crossref:special[using-python, 使用 Python]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2363
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`USES=python:env` can be used when the variables exported by the framework "
"are needed but a dependency on Python is not.  It can happen when using with "
"crossref:uses[uses-shebangfix,`USES=shebangfix`], and the goal is only to "
"fix the shebangs but not add a dependency on Python."
msgstr "如果需要框架导出的变量，但不需要依赖 Python，可以使用 `USES=python:env`。例如，与 crossref:uses[uses-shebangfix,`USES=shebangfix`] 配合使用时，目标可能只是修正 shebang，而不添加对 Python 的依赖。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2365
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`qmail`"
msgstr "`qmail`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2368
#, fuzzy
msgid "Possible arguments: (none), `build`, `run`, `both`, `vars`"
msgstr "可能的参数：（无）、`build`、`run`、`both`、`vars`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2373
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Uses package:mail/qmail[]. With the `build` argument, it implies `qmail` as "
"a build-time dependency.  `run` implies a run-time dependency.  Using no "
"argument or the `both` argument implies both run-time and build-time "
"dependencies.  `vars` will only set QMAIL variables for the port to use."
msgstr "使用 package:mail/qmail[]。使用 `build` 参数时，会将 `qmail` 设为构建时依赖；`run` 会将其设为运行时依赖。不带参数或使用 `both` 参数时，会同时添加运行时和构建时依赖。`vars` 仅设置供 Port 使用的 QMAIL 变量。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2375
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`qmake`"
msgstr "`qmake`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2378
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Possible arguments: (none), `norecursive`, `outsource`, `no_env`, "
"`no_configure`"
msgstr "可能的参数：（无）、`norecursive`、`outsource`、`no_env`、`no_configure`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2380
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Uses QMake for configuring. For more information see crossref:special[using-"
"qmake,Using `qmake`]."
msgstr "使用 QMake 进行配置。更多信息请参见 crossref:special[using-qmake,使用 `qmake`]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2385
#, fuzzy
msgid "Possible arguments: `5`, `6`, `no_env`"
msgstr "可能的参数：`5`、`6`、`no_env`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2389
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Add dependency on Qt components.  `no_env` is passed directly to `USES= "
"qmake`.  See crossref:special[using-qt,Using Qt] for more information."
msgstr "添加对 Qt 组件的依赖。`no_env` 会直接传递给 `USES= qmake`。更多信息请参见 crossref:special[using-qt,使用 Qt]。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2391
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`qt-dist`"
msgstr "`qt-dist`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/porters-handbook/uses/_index.adoc:2394
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Possible arguments: (none) or `5` and (none) or `6` and (none) or one of "
